Found three real defects; no style-only findings.

- **P1 — Elevated L3 authorization is lost across later commits.** With `--base`, `_gate_floor_paths` returns `pending_human=None`, assuming path classification captures all risk. That assumption is false for `--raise-tier`, whose purpose is risk the classifier cannot see. An unapproved elevated auth/config commit followed by an L1 commit can therefore pass CI at L1. The non-`--base` path has the same hole under `--human-gate-scope irreversible`, because ancestor authorization ignores `tier_source == "elevated"`. See [bin/coverloop:411](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:411), [bin/coverloop:439](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:439), and [bin/coverloop:2205](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2205). Carry unapproved elevated-L3 obligations through both paths and add a stacked-commit `--base` regression test.

- **P1 — The in-repo reviewer guard is bypassable.** The whitespace heuristic checks whether individual tokens resolve to regular files, but reviewer execution uses `shell=True` from the repository root. A trusted policy containing `python3 -m reviewer` can be hijacked by adding `reviewer.py` to the repository; `sh <scripts/reviewer` similarly evades detection because the checked token is `<scripts/reviewer`. The repository-controlled code can print `VERDICT: PASS`, defeating reviewer independence. See [bin/coverloop:999](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:999) and [bin/coverloop:2385](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2385). Arbitrary shell commands need isolation from the worktree, with the diff supplied explicitly.

- **P2 — `check --json` does not preserve JSON-only stdout.** `redirect_stdout` only redirects Python writes; the test subprocess inherits file descriptor 1 and can print before the JSON document. Nearly any normal test command therefore makes stdout invalid JSON. The regression fixture misses this because its command is silent `true`. See [bin/coverloop:1405](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1405), [bin/coverloop:2540](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2540), and [tests/test_properties.py:1850](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/tests/test_properties.py:1850).

