  2270	# The words real reviewers actually end on. Sampled from the fleet's captured
  2271	# transcripts: Codex ends "VERDICT: PASS", GLM's red-team scale is
  2272	# "Verdict: PASS / PASS WITH RISKS / REQUEST CHANGES / BLOCK", and some runs
  2273	# emit lowercase "verdict: fail" or a GitHub-style "APPROVE". A parser that
  2274	# only knew uppercase "VERDICT: PASS" scored every one of those a fail —
  2275	# fail-closed, but useless: it would have made `check` unusable with the very
  2276	# reviewers this repo ships. Unknown wording still fails.
  2277	# The reviewer's verdict is a MACHINE PROTOCOL, not prose to be interpreted.
  2278	# Exactly one canonical marker line counts:
  2279	#
  2280	#     VERDICT: PASS        (or)        VERDICT: FAIL

